4,5 $ Pileus surface squamulose; pileus covering made up either of long elements, or of inflated to rounded elements in chains

5,cs5 $ Pileus set with acute, pyramidal squamules, made up of agglutinated chains of elements, from cylindrical to inflated elements at base of squamules, gradually changing into ellipsoid to globose terminal elements (Fig. 79b) $$s "5-Key five"
5,cs6 $ Pileus set with squamules, made up of elongate, cylindrical elements, without or with septa, which are provided with or without clamp-connections (Fig. 79c, two types) $$s "6-Key six"


