15,0 $ All other combinations of characters: see discussion under L. echinella
15,0,N$///There appears to be huge variation in the main characters used to distinguish species in the vicinity of Lepiota echinella: spore size, shape of the cheilocysiidia and the length and structure of the elements of the pileus covering. Short characteristics of the existing species are given in the following overview, which is a compilation of literature on the existing names: the problems in interpretation of some names are outlined. Bon (FI. rnycol. Eur. 3, Lépiotes: 68-77. 1993) in his treatment of this group, emphasized colour of the basidiocarps, while here priority is given to microscopical characters.




